@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using System.Globalization
@using SpaceSails.Client.Rendering
@using SpaceSails.Contracts
@using SpaceSails.Core
@using SpaceSails.Core.Interior
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE HARDCASE CARD, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@* ── THE PAGE'S OWN NOTE ON THIS SURFACE, moved here with it (#251 item 1) and not touched by a
   word: it is the paragraph that stood above this block in Map.razor. It sits ABOVE the fence, not
   inside it, so that a source guard slicing the block by text goes on reading markup and not prose.
   ── *@
    @* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       #1061 beat 2 · BREM KOLT, HAZARDOUS ACCOUNTS. The same firm as the panel above and deliberately the
       same markup — one .rep-card, one scrim, one shell — because he is a salesman from Nebula Mutual and
       drawing him differently would be the page claiming a difference the fiction does not have.

       WHAT IS DIFFERENT IS TWO THINGS. There is NO PORTRAIT: Fess has the one portrait arc 2 allows, and
       hanging his face over Kolt's name would be the third named bug class with a photograph on it (the
       picture reporting a man the sim is not holding). Caption-only is #528's deliberate no-picture idiom
       and it is taken on purpose here, not by omission — no plate in this repository is a picture of him.
       And his line is TWO sentences, because the canon is two: the opener and the pitch, in that order.

       AND THE WAY OUT IS HIS REFUSAL. A ✕ that only took the panel away would leave a man standing at your
       elbow on open regolith with nothing left to answer — so the dismiss runs the verb "Not today" runs:
       he says the third line, and it is the only thing he has to say about being turned down.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ *@

@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="view-object-backdrop rep-backdrop">
            <OverlayShell class="view-object rep-card" StopClicks="true"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.Close"
                          DismissClass="view-object-close" DismissFace="Step away"
                          DismissLabel="Step away from the underwriter — the same as declining"
                          DismissTitle="Walk on without signing. He has one thing left to say about that"
                          OnClose="() => Dismiss(TellKoltNo)">
                <div class="view-object-title">@SpaceSails.Core.HardcaseRep.DisplayName</div>
                <div class="rep-desk">@SpaceSails.Core.HardcaseRep.Desk</div>
                <div class="view-object-caption rep-pitch">@SpaceSails.Core.HardcaseRep.Opener</div>
                <div class="view-object-caption rep-pitch">@SpaceSails.Core.HardcaseRep.Pitch</div>
                <div class="rep-offers">
                    @foreach (var koltOffer in koltOffers)
                    {
                        var koltMove = koltOffer.Move;
                        <button type="button" class="rep-offer" @onclick="() => Dismiss(() => AnswerTheHardcase(koltMove))">@koltOffer.Label</button>
                    }
                </div>
            </OverlayShell>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}
